// A bare name a submodule's import reaches as a FILE, which its parent answers
// with something else.
//
// An import asks the registry first. But a submodule is parsed before its
// parent's own files, so the parent's declarations cannot answer at parse, and
// a name a file answers is taken as that file there. Were the registry complete
// at parse it would have answered instead, so the two meaning different things
// is refused rather than decided by which was parsed first.
//
// The file is reached through the package search path, which this scenario's
// run adds: it is the group's own folder, so 'modulesub' is the support module.
// A path relative to the submodule reaches only its own files and submodules,
// which are refused on their own terms (ErrorModFile).
//
// The folder holds:
//   sub/sub.cone   imports modulesub by its bare name

mod module_import_parent_file;

// Not a module: a function of this module that the name also answers to
fn modulesub() i64 {
  1i64;
}

fn designated() i64 {
  modulesub();
}
